<title>NETHERLANDS: KLM mulls stake in Indonesian Garuda - paper.</title>
<headline>KLM mulls stake in Indonesian Garuda - paper.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch flag carrier KLM is considering taking a 25 percent stake in state-owned Indonesian airline Garuda, due to be privatised in 1998, newspaper De Telegraaf said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Quoting Garuda officials in Jakarta it said Indonesia's transport minister had held talks with KLM chairman Pieter Bouw over extending the co-operation pact between the two airlines. No financial details of any potential stake were given.</p>
<p>The paper adeed Indonesian officials had also held talks with Germany's Lufthansa, British Airways and Air France.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
